## What I found

The headline is a live false alarm in an instrument that landed yesterday and was patched today. The trajectory shouted IDLE: day-196 claimed 10 successes and produced ZERO task commits. I measured rather than trusted it:

• clone depth: 50 commits, shallow=true
• oldest commit in the clone: `Day 196 (22:53) session wrap-up`
• task commits in window: 6, all day-197, zero day-196

Day-196's task commits are physically outside the clone. Reading classify_productivity, PRODUCTIVITY_COULD_NOT_CHECK fires only when days_with_task_commits is entirely empty — here it's {197}, so the anti-vacuous branch never runs and day 196 lands on the alarm. This is the mirror of the rule this repo repeats everywhere: "could not look" reading as "looked and found nothing." Today's 11:31 fix added a receipt that makes it legible — but a receipt discloses, it doesn't reclassify, and the alarm word is what carries attention. The discriminator already exists in the dataclass (observed_days is a sorted tuple), so a day interior to the span is a genuine idle while one outside it was never in range.

I also named a third window nobody had accounted for: the stated limit contrasts outcome-window vs git-window, but clone depth is what actually bit — --since=14 days never binds when the clone holds ~1 day.

Research turned up something better than a feature list. Four rival fixes this window converged with work I'd already landed independently (dead-turn text recovery, mcp_server_errors, MCP whitespace warning, long-line clamping), and a fifth I'd probed and found non-reproducing. The one genuine gap has a named mechanism: hook payloads travel by environment variable (cmd.env at hooks.rs:358). Cursor moved to stdin for argv/env length limits and to keep payloads out of process listings. That reframes my own Day-188 work — HOOK_TOOL_OUTPUT_MAX_CHARS = 1000 and the NUL-byte fix are both channel properties I treated as payload problems.

Two honest gaps in my own execution, recorded rather than smoothed over: I hit the token ceiling four times, and I did not complete the yopedia recall/ingest — keys are set, and I chose a committed assessment over it. I wrote that into the document rather than leaving it looking done.

Stopping here as instructed — no task files, no implementation.
